#DESCRIPTION
Intrinsic magnetic field with a CONDUCTING inner body: the total field is made
tangential to the surface, the intrinsic field passes through it.

Same isolated setup as the .body deck (SOLVEEM F, zero UNIFORMSTATE field), with
a BODY of radius 1 at the origin and a tilted dipole. The only difference is the
field boundary condition: 'conducting' instead of 'linetied', so the surface
condition applies and the evolved field B1 is no longer identically zero.

Because B1 starts at zero, the surface condition n . (B1 + B0) = 0 forces
B1 = -B0.n n-hat exactly on the surface shell, and nothing anywhere else. That
makes the deck a sharp test of the split:

  * on the shell     the TOTAL field is tangential (B_r = 0 to round-off),
  * off the shell    B1 stays zero, so B_total = B0 is untouched,
  * inside the body  B0 still exists and E = 0,
  * B0 does not evolve and the magnetic energy is constant.

This is the condition BATSRUS calls 'reflectb', where the ghost state is built
from B + B0 before being reflected so that the face average of the total field
is tangential. Before this, FLEKS rejected the combination outright because it
pinned B1.n to zero and a dipole necessarily crosses the surface.

